### TITLE ###
ARuntimeErrorDoesNotEndTheSession
### DESCRIPTION ###
The behavior the REPL exists to have. The diagnostic is the same one a script
would print, the exit code is still zero, and the variable defined before the
error is still there afterwards.
### ARGS ###
repl
### STDIN ###
x = 5
undefined_variable
x
print("still here")
### NO_TERMINAL ###
### STDOUT ###
🤙 Rad REPL v0.11.0
Type ':help' for help, ':exit' or Ctrl+D to quit.

5
still here
### STDERR ###
error[RAD20028]: Undefined variable: undefined_variable
  --> <repl>:1:1
  |
1 | undefined_variable
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  |
  = info: rad docs RAD20028

### TITLE ###
ASyntaxErrorDoesNotEndTheSessionEither
### DESCRIPTION ###
Syntax diagnostics are borrowed from the checker so they name the offending
text, exactly as they do for a file. The rest of the checker is skipped: it
rebuilds its scope from the buffer alone, so it would report every variable
from an earlier turn as undefined.
### ARGS ###
repl
### STDIN ###
x = 1
this is not rad!!!
x
### NO_TERMINAL ###
### STDOUT ###
🤙 Rad REPL v0.11.0
Type ':help' for help, ':exit' or Ctrl+D to quit.

1
### STDERR ###
error[RAD10009]: Unexpected 'this is not rad!!!'
  --> <repl>:1:1
  |
1 | this is not rad!!!
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  |
  = info: rad docs RAD10009

error[RAD10009]: Unexpected 'is'
  --> <repl>:1:6
  |
1 | this is not rad!!!
  |      ^^
  |
  = info: rad docs RAD10009

error[RAD10001]: Expected 'in'
  --> <repl>:1:12
  |
1 | this is not rad!!!
  |            ^
  |
  = info: rad docs RAD10001

error[RAD10009]: Unexpected '!!!'
  --> <repl>:1:16
  |
1 | this is not rad!!!
  |                ^^^
  |
  = info: rad docs RAD10009

### TITLE ###
ErrorsInsideBlocksRecoverToo
### DESCRIPTION ###
The unwind leaves the environment intact, so a loop that dies part-way through
keeps whatever it managed to assign.
### ARGS ###
repl
### STDIN ###
total = 0
for i in range(3):
    total = total + i
    missing_fn(i)

total
### NO_TERMINAL ###
### STDOUT ###
🤙 Rad REPL v0.11.0
Type ':help' for help, ':exit' or Ctrl+D to quit.

0
### STDERR ###
error[RAD40003]: Cannot invoke unknown function: missing_fn
  --> <repl>:3:5
  |
2 |     total = total + i
3 |     missing_fn(i)
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^
  |
  = info: rad docs RAD40003

### TITLE ###
CatchStillHandlesWhatItShould
### DESCRIPTION ###
Recovering from a fatal error at the turn boundary must not swallow the errors
user code meant to handle itself.
### ARGS ###
repl
### STDIN ###
result = int("abc") catch:
    result = -1

result
### NO_TERMINAL ###
### STDOUT ###
🤙 Rad REPL v0.11.0
Type ':help' for help, ':exit' or Ctrl+D to quit.

-1
